@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>IPCamLapse is a local-first application. It does not include analytics, advertising, telemetry, or cloud storage.</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Data stored on this computer</h2>
<p>Session settings, camera URLs, usernames, capture timestamps, JPEG frames, and generated videos are stored below the application's <code>data/sessions</code> directory. Camera passwords are protected at rest with ASP.NET Core Data Protection, but the running application can access them when it connects to a camera.</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Browser data</h2>
<p>The application uses an anti-forgery cookie to protect state-changing requests. It does not use tracking cookies.</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Network requests</h2>
<p>At runtime, IPCamLapse connects only to the camera endpoints you configure. Anyone exposing the app through a reverse proxy is responsible for that proxy's authentication, logging, and privacy practices.</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Deleting data</h2>
<p>Deleting a session removes its metadata, captured images, and generated videos from the session storage directory. Normal file-system backup and recovery tools may retain copies outside IPCamLapse's control.</p>
